# Pure derived artefacts of docs/derived/architecture-map/{ancore.mjs,build.mjs}.
# See docs/derived/architecture-map/README.md and setup-merge-driver.mjs.
#
# `merge=mappa-regen` is configured locally (never here — Git requires a
# driver definition to live in `.git/config`) as the builtin `true` command:
# on a conflict, Git just keeps "ours" instead of leaving a human to
# textually merge 289 KB of generated JSON/HTML. The real content is
# recomputed correctly a moment later, once the whole merge/rebase has
# finished (`post-merge-regen.mjs`, wired via `.githooks/post-merge` and
# `post-rewrite`) — not mid-merge, when sibling files this map cites are not
# guaranteed to be on disk yet.
#
# Every clone gets this registered automatically on `npm install` / `npm ci`
# via the `prepare` script. A clone that never ran it keeps Git's normal
# 3-way text merge on these two paths: today's behaviour, never a silent
# wrong merge.
docs/derived/architecture-map/ancore.json merge=mappa-regen
docs/derived/architecture-map/mappa.html merge=mappa-regen -diff linguist-generated=true
